# Build-context exclusions.
#
# SECURITY: the backend Dockerfile does `COPY backend/ ./`. Without this file
# `backend/.env` -- which holds the live provider API key -- would be copied
# into an image layer, where it survives `docker history`, layer extraction and
# any push to a registry. Deleting the file in a later layer would not remove
# it. Secrets reach the container through `environment:` in docker-compose,
# never through the image.

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*

# --- Local databases --------------------------------------------------------
# A development database contains real conversations and memories.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
**/*.db

# --- Virtualenvs and caches -------------------------------------------------
# Host-built wheels are the wrong platform, and .venv is ~49MB of noise that
# would also invalidate the layer cache on every local install.
.venv/
venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# --- Node -------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
**/.next/

# --- VCS and tooling --------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
*.log

# --- Docs and editors -------------------------------------------------------
docs/
*.md
!README.md
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# --- Tests ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The suite is not needed to serve a request, and shipping it puts thousands
# of lines of fixtures into the production image -- including the synthetic
# sentinel credentials the security tests use, which are harmless but which
# make an image scan look alarming and bury a real finding if one ever
# appears. Stage 4G.1 removed pytest from the image for the same reason.
#
# Development is unaffected: docker-compose bind-mounts ./backend over /app.
backend/tests/
backend/requirements-dev.txt

# Runtime workspace. Never built into an image.
mai_workspace/
backend/mai_workspace/

# Never copy a credential store into an image.
.mai/
credentials/
